he Kconfig/Twister setup and FIFO test):*\n```\ndriver: accelgyro_lsm6dso: Fix set_range() accel normalization and error return\n\nIn set_range(), accelerometer inputs were passed to\nLSM6DSO_ACCEL_NORMALIZE_FS() (__fls()) before clamping to the supported\n[2G, 16G] range, the round-up check used `\u003c` instead of `\u003e` (never\nrounding up non-power-of-two inputs), and ranges were not normalized to\na power of two before computing the register value and updating\ncurrent_range. In addition, set_range() unconditionally returned\nEC_SUCCESS, masking I2C write failures from callers.\n\nClamp requested accelerometer ranges to [2G, 16G], normalize to a power\nof two (doubling when rounding up is requested), and return the status\nfrom st_write_data_with_mask().\n\nBUG\u003db:574009721\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.lsm6dso\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/e6dd4432-46cd-4def-bb54-ce54a455b610)",
