      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Please split this CL into focused changes, simplify the accelerometer normalization control flow in `set_range()`, expand unit test coverage, and update the commit message.\n\n### Review Summary\n- **Functionality:** ✅ Clamping accelerometer ranges to `[LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL]`, fixing the round-up comparison to `\u003e`, normalizing to a power of two, and propagating `err` from `set_range()` address the underlying driver defects.\n- **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** ✅ Defining `LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL` in `driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso.h` aligns with sibling ST motion sensor drivers (`accelgyro_lsm6dsm.h`).\n- **Code Simplicity:** ❌ In `set_range()`, normalizing the clamped `range` via `LSM6DSO_ACCEL_NORMALIZE_FS(range)` before checking `rnd` avoids calling `__fls()` twice and eliminates the subsequent `if (newrange \u003e LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL) ... else ...` branch. In `zephyr/test/drivers/Kconfig`, `default n` on a `bool` symbol is redundant.\n- **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** ❌ `test_set_range_rounding_clamping` passes a magic number (`10000000`) instead of deriving from `LSM6DSO_GYRO_NORMALIZE_FS(LSM6DSO_GYRO_FS_MAX_REG_VAL)`, and `test_push_fifo_data_oob_tags` uses a magic `0xFF` tag literal instead of deriving from `enum lsm6dso_tag_fifo`.\n- **Security:** ✅ No security vulnerabilities introduced.\n- **Testing:** ❌ `test_set_range_rounding_clamping` is missing test cases for: (1) `set_range()` I2C write error propagation (`return err`), (2) clamping below/at `LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL`, (3) rounding down (`rnd \u003d 0`) on non-power-of-two inputs, (4) `rnd \u003d 1` on exact power-of-two boundaries and `LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL - 1`, and (5) asserting `gyro-\u003ecurrent_range` after clamping gyro range to max.\n- **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** ❌ `Size: M (+59, -2)` (7 lines production diff, 54 lines test/config diff). While small in line count, this CL bundles four independent logical changes that should be split into separate CLs:\n  1. **CL 1:** Wire up `CONFIG_LINK_TEST_SUITE_LSM6DSO` in `zephyr/test/drivers/Kconfig` and register `drivers.lsm6dso` in `zephyr/test/drivers/testcase.yaml`.\n  2. **CL 2:** Add `test_push_fifo_data_oob_tags` in `zephyr/test/drivers/lsm6dso/src/main.c` covering out-of-bounds FIFO tag handling in `push_fifo_data()`.\n  3. **CL 3:** Fix `set_range()` in `driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso.c` to return `err` instead of `EC_SUCCESS`, with its unit test in `zephyr/test/drivers/lsm6dso/src/main.c`.\n  4. **CL 4:** Fix `set_range()` accelerometer full-scale clamping, rounding, and normalization in `driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso.h` and `driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso.c`, with boundary unit tests in `zephyr/test/drivers/lsm6dso/src/main.c`.\n- **Commit Message:** ❌ The commit message narrates the code diff without stating the *Why* (problem statement), omits the `Kconfig`/`testcase.yaml` and `test_push_fifo_data_oob_tags` changes, and lists `TEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.default` instead of `drivers.lsm6dso`. [🔗](http://go/tj/e6dd4432-46cd-4def-bb54-ce54a455b610)",
