      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Since `range` is clamped to `[LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL]` (`[2, 16]`) first, normalizing to the floor power of two (`newrange \u003d LSM6DSO_ACCEL_NORMALIZE_FS(range)`) before checking `rnd` simplifies the control flow:\n\n- When `range \u003d\u003d 16`, `newrange` is `16`, so `range \u003e newrange` is `false`.\n- When `range \u003c 16` (`range \u003c\u003d 15`), `newrange` is at most `8`; doubling `newrange` when `rnd \u0026\u0026 (range \u003e newrange)` yields at most `16` (`LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL`) and is already a normalized power of two.\n\nThis avoids evaluating `LSM6DSO_ACCEL_NORMALIZE_FS()` (`__fls()`) twice and eliminates the second `if (newrange \u003e LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL) ... else ...` branch (matching the normalize-then-round pattern used in `set_data_rate()` below):\n\n```c\n\tif (s-\u003etype \u003d\u003d MOTIONSENSE_TYPE_ACCEL) {\n\t\trange \u003d CLAMP(range, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL,\n\t\t\t      LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL);\n\n\t\t/* Adjust and check rounded value for Acc. */\n\t\tnewrange \u003d LSM6DSO_ACCEL_NORMALIZE_FS(range);\n\t\tif (rnd \u0026\u0026 (range \u003e newrange))\n\t\t\tnewrange *\u003d 2;\n\n\t\treg_val \u003d lsm6dso_accel_fs_reg(newrange);\n\t} else {\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/e6dd4432-46cd-4def-bb54-ce54a455b610)",
