      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] `test_push_fifo_data_oob_tags` tests out-of-bounds FIFO tag handling in `push_fifo_data()` / `irq_handler()`, which is unrelated to the `set_range()` fix in this CL. Please move this test to a separate CL (or to the CL that modified `push_fifo_data()`).\n\nWhen moving this test, please also:\n1. Replace the magic `0xFF` literal with a named constant derived from `enum lsm6dso_tag_fifo` (e.g., `const uint8_t invalid_tag \u003d (LSM6DSO_ACC_TAG + 1) \u003c\u003c 3;`).\n2. Assert the postcondition that `irq_handler()` drained the FIFO sample from `LSM6DSO_FIFO_STS1_ADDR` rather than only asserting `zassert_ok(...)`:\n\n```c\nZTEST(lsm6dso, test_push_fifo_data_oob_tags)\n{\n\tconst uint16_t initial_fifo_len \u003d 1;\n\tconst uint8_t invalid_tag \u003d (LSM6DSO_ACC_TAG + 1) \u003c\u003c 3;\n\tuint32_t event \u003d CONFIG_ACCEL_LSM6DSO_INT_EVENT;\n\tint sts \u003d 0xFF;\n\n\tzassert_ok(i2c_write16(acc-\u003eport, acc-\u003ei2c_spi_addr_flags,\n\t\t\t       LSM6DSO_FIFO_STS1_ADDR, initial_fifo_len));\n\tzassert_ok(i2c_write8(acc-\u003eport, acc-\u003ei2c_spi_addr_flags,\n\t\t\t      LSM6DSO_FIFO_DATA_ADDR_TAG, invalid_tag));\n\n\tzassert_ok(acc-\u003edrv-\u003eirq_handler(acc, \u0026event));\n\tzassert_ok(i2c_read8(acc-\u003eport, acc-\u003ei2c_spi_addr_flags,\n\t\t\t     LSM6DSO_FIFO_STS1_ADDR, \u0026sts));\n\tzassert_equal(sts \u0026 LSM6DSO_FIFO_DIFF_MASK, 0);\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/e6dd4432-46cd-4def-bb54-ce54a455b610)",
