      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Please expand `test_set_range_rounding_clamping` (and add an error-propagation test) to cover all modified branches, boundaries, and postconditions in `set_range()`:\n\n1. **Missing Error-Propagation Test (`return err`):** `set_range()` was updated to return `err` instead of `EC_SUCCESS`, but no test verifies that an I2C write failure on `LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_ADDR` returns an error and leaves `current_range` unchanged.\n2. **Missing Lower-Bound Clamping, Round-Down (`rnd \u003d 0`), and Exact-Boundary Cases:**\n   - Clamping below and at the minimum (`0`, `LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL - 1`, `LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL`) is not tested.\n   - Rounding down (`rnd \u003d 0`) for a non-power-of-two input (`LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL + 1` -\u003e `LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL`) is not tested, leaving the normalization path for `rnd \u003d 0` unverified.\n   - Calling `set_range()` with `rnd \u003d 1` on exact power-of-two boundaries (`LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL` and `LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL`) and just below the max (`LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL - 1` -\u003e `LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL`) is not tested (needed to ensure `\u003e` does not round up exact powers of two and caps at `LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL`).\n3. **Missing Postcondition Assertion \u0026 Magic Number on Gyro Clamping (lines 88–89):** `zassert_ok(gyro-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(gyro, 10000000, 0));` does not assert `gyro-\u003ecurrent_range`, and uses the magic literal `10000000` instead of deriving from `LSM6DSO_GYRO_NORMALIZE_FS(LSM6DSO_GYRO_FS_MAX_REG_VAL)`.\n4. **Restore Initial Sensor State:** Save and restore `acc-\u003ecurrent_range` and `gyro-\u003ecurrent_range` so test state does not leak to other tests in the suite.\n\n```c\nZTEST(lsm6dso, test_set_range_rounding_clamping)\n{\n\tstruct motion_sensor_t *gyro \u003d \u0026motion_sensors[GYR_SENSOR_ID];\n\tconst int orig_acc_range \u003d acc-\u003ecurrent_range;\n\tconst int orig_gyro_range \u003d gyro-\u003ecurrent_range;\n\tconst int gyro_max_range \u003d\n\t\tLSM6DSO_GYRO_NORMALIZE_FS(LSM6DSO_GYRO_FS_MAX_REG_VAL);\n\n\t/* Test accel clamping below and at min */\n\tzassert_ok(acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(acc, 0, 0));\n\tzassert_equal(acc-\u003ecurrent_range, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL);\n\tzassert_ok(acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(acc, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL - 1, 1));\n\tzassert_equal(acc-\u003ecurrent_range, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL);\n\n\t/* Exact power-of-two boundary with rnd\u003d1 should not round up */\n\tzassert_ok(acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(acc, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL, 1));\n\tzassert_equal(acc-\u003ecurrent_range, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL);\n\n\t/* Non-power-of-two with rnd\u003d0 should round down */\n\tzassert_ok(acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(acc, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL + 1, 0));\n\tzassert_equal(acc-\u003ecurrent_range, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL);\n\n\t/* Non-power-of-two with rnd\u003d1 should round up to next power of 2 */\n\tzassert_ok(acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(acc, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL + 1, 1));\n\tzassert_equal(acc-\u003ecurrent_range, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL * 2);\n\n\t/* Near-max with rnd\u003d1 and clamping above max */\n\tzassert_ok(acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(acc, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL - 1, 1));\n\tzassert_equal(acc-\u003ecurrent_range, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL);\n\tzassert_ok(acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(acc, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL, 1));\n\tzassert_equal(acc-\u003ecurrent_range, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL);\n\tzassert_ok(acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(acc, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL + 1, 0));\n\tzassert_equal(acc-\u003ecurrent_range, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL);\n\n\t/* Test gyro clamping to max and rounding up */\n\tzassert_ok(gyro-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(gyro, gyro_max_range * 2, 0));\n\tzassert_equal(gyro-\u003ecurrent_range, gyro_max_range);\n\tzassert_ok(gyro-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(gyro, LSM6DSO_GYRO_NORMALIZE_FS(0) + 1,\n\t\t\t\t\t1));\n\tzassert_equal(gyro-\u003ecurrent_range, LSM6DSO_GYRO_NORMALIZE_FS(1));\n\n\t/* Restore original ranges */\n\tzassert_ok(acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(acc, orig_acc_range, 0));\n\tzassert_ok(gyro-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(gyro, orig_gyro_range, 0));\n}\n\nZTEST(lsm6dso, test_set_range_write_error)\n{\n\tconst int orig_acc_range \u003d acc-\u003ecurrent_range;\n\n\tzassert_ok(acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(acc, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL, 0));\n\tlsm6dso_emul_set_write_fail_reg(emul, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_ADDR);\n\n\tzassert_equal(EC_ERROR_INVAL,\n\t\t      acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(acc, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL, 0));\n\tzassert_equal(acc-\u003ecurrent_range, LSM6DSO_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL);\n\n\tlsm6dso_emul_set_write_fail_reg(emul, -1);\n\tzassert_ok(acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_range(acc, orig_acc_range, 0));\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/e6dd4432-46cd-4def-bb54-ce54a455b610)",
